  "body": "Stacked on #147 (issue/112-coolant). Retarget to main before #147 merges.\n\n## What changed\n\nFollow-ups from #147's review (#150):\n1. All six posts' coolant refusals start with `operation <name>:`.\n2. The machine editor's coolant name is a dropdown (Flood, Mist, Through-spindle, Through-tool, from `machine::COOLANT_KINDS`) plus \"custom\" (e.g. `Brine`). Posts accept spelling variants such as \"Through spindle\". The accepted names are listed in `assets/machines/AGENTS.md`.\n3. A Flood op is refused by name when the machine lists coolants but none of them is flood (before, it posted M7 on a mist-only machine). **Decision to check:** a machine with *no* coolant list, or a Flood entry with no M-code (manual coolant), still posts with no coolant word. Blocking those would stop every program on such machines. See RECOMMENDED.md.\n4. Posts declare `coolantModes = true` when they read `PARAM Coolant`; all shipped posts do. Without the flag, the engine refuses any Off, Mist or Through-tool op by name. Flood-only programs and user posts are unchanged.\n5. The owed tests.\n\n## Pins\n\n- New `coolant_followups.rs` (7): coolant per section on Fanuc Lathe, M88 on the shipped mill-turn, Mist→Flood on every mill post, plus items 1–4.\n- ui: the dropdown click test.\n\n## Readings\n\ncoolant 7, coolant_followups 7, conformance 5, posting 17, fanuc_post 8, lathe_post 5, machine 32, camcraft-post all, ui lib 238; clippy is clean; default-Flood goldens unchanged.\n\nChangelog: Coolant refusals name the operation; a Flood op on a machine that lists no flood code is refused; the machine editor picks coolant kinds; a post without coolantModes refuses non-Flood ops\n\nFixes #150\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
